# DISABLED EXAMPLE. Rename to 50-recurring-deliveries.caddy inside the
# gateway's /etc/caddy/routes.d/ to send this group to Rust.
#
# backend-rs/src/routes/recurring_deliveries.rs (a NEW feature, Rust only):
#   GET, POST   /api/v1/recurring-deliveries
#   POST        /api/v1/recurring-deliveries/preview
#   GET, PATCH  /api/v1/recurring-deliveries/{id}
#   POST        /api/v1/recurring-deliveries/{id}/status
#
# NO PYTHON FAILOVER: Python has no such route, so `api:8010` is deliberately
# NOT listed as a second upstream. With api-rs down these paths answer 502 (the
# frontend shows the load error); everything else keeps working. The schedules'
# materialiser loop also lives in the api-rs process: when it is down, no new
# commitments are generated and `/health` shows `recurring_deliveries` going
# stale. Rows already materialised keep counting in Python.

@rs_recurring_deliveries {
	path /api/v1/recurring-deliveries /api/v1/recurring-deliveries/*
}
handle @rs_recurring_deliveries {
	reverse_proxy api-rs:8021 {
		lb_try_duration 2s
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
